1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
Left is a real SAP system. Right is erpl-rev top, untouched.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:11,000
This is the ABAP that drives the demo. It has three branches.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Branch one posts a goods receipt. A plain INSERT. No API, no exit.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:20,500
Branch two transfers two items. One UPDATE, one unit of work.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:26,000
Branch three deletes a row physically. No flag, no tombstone.

6
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:32,200
SAP contains one million goods movements. DuckDB contains none.

7
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:43,200
The sync starts. The left pane prints nothing. The graph shows the rate.

8
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:51,200
Colour is the target. The glyph is the operation. Up means insert.

9
00:00:55,200 --> 00:01:01,200
One million rows in 11 seconds. About 91,000 per second, on a laptop.

10
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Ten rows from end to end of the table. Real documents, real quantities.

11
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:22,400
A live change. The goods receipt is posted in SAP. Nothing runs here.

12
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:30,400
Three items arrive two seconds later. One cell: too small to measure.

13
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:40,900
The transfer moves two items to storage location 0002. One UPDATE.

14
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:50,400
Two updates. The row count does not change. The cycle reports them.

15
00:01:51,900 --> 00:02:00,900
The archiving run deletes item 0003. The row is gone from SAP.

16
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:07,400
A watermark cannot see this. Trigger CDC can. The graph draws a delete.

17
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:21,400
SAP trigger time against apply time in DuckDB. The gap is under 2.4 s.

18
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:32,200
Now thirty seconds of ordinary traffic. Postings, corrections, archiving.

19
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:41,200
About twenty rows per second. A mid-size site's volume, not a benchmark.

20
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:50,200
All three glyphs at once. The table is written and pruned at the same time.

21
00:02:50,200 --> 00:03:02,200
The left pane stays silent. The program only prints when it returns.

22
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:17,200
644 operations in SAP. Fewer changes applied: corrections inside one cycle arrive once.
